Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840 size patch to user/hamnix/hamsh.ad (the committed file plus the teensy41 patch's changes, which it repeats).
Applied by scripts/mkroot.sh in build/feather-nrf52840/root only; the
committed file is unchanged.

Reason: the nRF52840 has 256 KiB of RAM for everything: kernel data, kernel
stacks and heap, the files in / and every running program's stack and data
(boards/feather_nrf52840/link.ld; programs' code stays in flash).

On top of the teensy41 sizes (AST nodes, values, list elements 256; kid
slots 512; strings 8 KiB; history 4 lines; functions 64 -> here 16):

    input line, edited line, history slot   2048 -> 512 bytes
    history ring                            4 -> 2 lines
    tokens per logical input                256 -> 128
    argv slots (exec takes <= 64 strings)   256 -> 64
    environment entries                     32 -> 8
    user functions                          64 -> 16
    aliases                                 512 -> 32
    jobs                                    32 -> 8
    services (no service manager here)      32 -> 2, listing 512 bytes,
                                            spawn argv 256 bytes
    script / rc / $(...) capture buffers    8 / 4 / 4 KiB -> 1 KiB each
    glob listing, completion scratch        8 / 4 KiB -> 1 KiB / 512 bytes
    newshell passwd buffer                  4 KiB -> 256 bytes
    interned strings and the collector's    8 -> 4 KiB each (teensy41: 8;
    staging copy                            Hamnix: 128 / 64 KiB)
The shell's data: 219 -> about 100 KiB (measured: docs/boards/feather-nrf52840.md).

Only constants, array lengths, and messages that quote them change.
Generated by editing a copy and
    diff -u --label a/user/hamnix/hamsh.ad --label b/user/hamnix/hamsh.ad user/hamnix/hamsh.ad <copy>

